<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guerrero</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guerrero is a state of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> on the Pacific coast, with Chilpancingo as its capital and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acapulco">Acapulco</a> as its largest city. Its rugged Sierra Madre del Sur was home to the Yopes (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlapanec-people">Tlapanecs</a>) and other peoples, some never subdued by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a>. The state was created in 1849 and named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicente-guerrero">Vicente Guerrero</a>, a hero of the War of Independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guerrero.jpg" alt="Guerrero" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Comisión Mexicana de Filmaciones from México D. F., México · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zona_Arqueol%C3%B3gica_Tehuacalco,_Chilpancingo,_Guerrero-_Tehuacalco_Arqueologic_Zone,_Guerrero_(24832596181).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
